## Return Early Pattern

Use guard clauses to handle edge cases and failure conditions at the top of a function. Return immediately rather than nesting the happy path inside conditionals.

Good:
```
function process(data):
    if data is null: return
    if not data.is_valid(): return
    return do_work(data)
```

Bad:
```
function process(data):
    if data is not null:
        if data.is_valid():
            return do_work(data)
```

Apply this only where it genuinely reduces complexity.

Preserve simple if/else structures that are already clear.

Do not force the pattern into short functions where a single if/else reads better, or where the conditions represent legitimate alternative behaviours rather than failure cases.
